  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "bXnRjRgZw9sy"
   },
   "source": [
    "# Dysbiosis Index (DI) and Cliff Delta Index\n",
    " The DI provides a numerical value to quantify the extent of dysbiosis (microbial imbalance) in the gut, helping to differentiate between healthy and diarrhea. Cliff Delta is a non-parametric effect size statistic used to quantify the difference between two groups. Please refer to file [Dysbiosis and Cliff Index Analysis](Dysbiosis_Cliff_Index.R)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "os8Ickq5GqEe"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "install.packages("effsize") \n"
   ]
  },
